The family inverse-generates maximal standard monomials of native monomial ideals, based on Sections 2–4 of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/0806.3680v1).

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000; exact density ≈ `1.12e-11`.
- Six attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 7,680 pair inspections and 15,240 endpoint comparisons.
- Compact route: at most 256 field operations.
- Witness: 16 atoms, at most 77 characters.
- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 invariant transformations and 20/20 distinct unrelated instances.

The result is not yet shippable: every required OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving zero completed oracle attempts and no `hardened` verdict. The error transcripts are retained honestly. Restore the OpenRouter quota, rerun the bare and two G9 harness arms, then regenerate `selftest_report.json`.
